WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.580
<i>Looking at these, it's hard to ignore the intensity of the election.</i>

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.730
<i>I'll have to brace myself and go for the win.</i>

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.320
Do I even have a chance?

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.940
What the hell is this?

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.540
P-Please help me!

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.560
Wh-What the...

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.960
That scared me.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.270
Sorry, Aomi-san. I wasn't looking where I was going.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.840
Were you looking at those?

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.310
W-Well, yeah.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:12.800
You're amazing, Oojima-senpai,

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.760
You're going to be the Student Council President.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.500
Well, I haven't gotten there yet.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:18.910
In fact, I doubt I will.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.660
The fact that you're going for it is amazing enough!

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.240
You have my support!

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.780
Thank you, Aomi-san.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:27.290
By the way, what were you doing?

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:29.280
Maintenance for the school.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.830
The factory's closed today,

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.240
and I didn't want to waste my free time doing nothing.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:36.380
I see.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.360
Being a financial aid student must be tough.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:44.510
Actually, it's thanks to the financial aid system that I can study here.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:50.440
I have two little brothers, so I would be out of school to work otherwise.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.800
You smell something?

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:53.690
Yeah, something stinks.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.800
Maybe someone didn't take a bath?

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.400
People who don't have the money shouldn't try so hard to come to Takafuji.

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:01.950
Are they your classmates?

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.870
I'll go tell them off.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:06.980
It's fine!

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.530
This will only get worse if you don't do anything!

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:11.860
It's fine.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:14.240
Those guys have always been that way.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.550
Always? They've <i>always</i> been like that?

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.750
Those bastards!

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.740
A-Anyway, can I ask you something?

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:22.430
Huh?

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:26.220
Um, do I really stink?

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:32.800
They always say I stink, so I've started
to think that maybe I really do...

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:33.940
Of course you don't!

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.230
They're just harassing—

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.480
Please don't just try to console me. Tell me the truth!

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:41.900
A-Aomi-san?

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.910
Senpai, please!

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.200
U-Um...

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.400
Th-Then...

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.670
W-Well?

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.880
What a sublime scent!

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.970
S-So do I stink?

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.180
Not at all! In fact...

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:07.920
In fact?

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.220
Oh, no, never mind.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.930
Aomi-san, you don't stink at all.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.640
I guarantee it!

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.770
That's a relief.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.020
Thank you very much, Senpai!

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.380
No, the pleasure is all mine.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:21.140
Sorry?

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:22.950
Oh, nothing.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.950
Oojima
Yuuki
Election
Headquarters<b></b>

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:29.080
So it <i>is</i> true that election campaigns cost a lot of money.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.760
We need to find funding.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.080
We don't have any money, after all.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.780
Apparently, the Finance, General Affairs, and Public Safety Commissions—

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:37.060
the three administrative organizations—

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.340
receive campaign funds from the school.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.900
Must be nice to be them.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.460
Yeah, it really was a nice smell.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:45.280
What?

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:46.590
Nothing.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:50.900
The people who spend a lot of money on an election are special-interests up to no good, right?

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.850
We should run a clean election campaign without spending too much.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.230
Nevertheless, it would still cost us money.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:02.240
For example, how much do you think it would cost to hand out a flyer to every student?

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.820
Assuming the copying costs 10 yen per page,

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:08.410
for 6,000 people, it would cost 60,000 yen!

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.380
Indeed.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:14.830
Even with a low unit cost, you still require a large sum of money when appealing to the masses.

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:20.080
They say it costs the city council tens of millions of yen every year

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.860
just to send out the dozens of telegrams for weddings and funerals every day.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:26.220
So as an overall estimate, we'll need at least 30,000 yen.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.590
We should try to get around 50,000 yen if possible.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.700
How about covering it with the Food Club's funds?

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.100
You can't.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.100
Club funds are for club activities only.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.350
Using it for the election campaign would be considered misappropriation.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.780
What they don't know won't hurt them.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.980
If it came to light, any victory would be null and void.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.110
Moreover, the group in charge of such investigations is...

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.020
...the Finance Commission, huh?

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.860
Well, they'd definitely find us out.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.830
Our current options are...

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.240
Self-funding, huh?

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.360
We'd have 40,000 yen if each
of us contributed 5,000 yen.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.660
5,000 yen?!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:03.000
I can't! I don't have any allowance left for this month!

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.520
I don't have enough at the moment, either.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:10.100
A couple thousand yen might be reasonable,
but 5,000 yen per person is too much.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.760
Then you'll have to go with the second option.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:15.160
The bazaar?

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:18.640
The bazaar held during the primaries was originally instituted

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.770
as a way of raising campaign funds.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.920
So that's what it was for?

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:29.030
Some years ago, they raised the issue that people without money couldn't even run.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.460
The school doesn't allow part-time jobs.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:36.410
So they started the bazaar as a way of raising funds.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:41.290
And before long, the bazaar became the main event.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:47.670
We'll return the bazaar to its roots and use it to raise campaign funds.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.860
In that case, we'd need a hot item to sell.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:54.300
Non-chan strongly recommends
sales of the Oojima Roll!

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.620
Oojima Roll?

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:56.470
That's right!

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:00.230
Yuu-chan's specialty roll cake that can only be found at the Food club!

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:04.080
Fluffy sponge cake and fluffy cream in complete harmony!

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.460
It melts away the instant you take a bite,

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:11.440
filling your mouth with its heavenly
sweetness and refreshing scent!

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:14.940
Then the fruits emerge from the layer of cream

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:18.800
in a symphony of mouthwatering flavor with just the right sourness!

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.700
It is, without a doubt, the ultimate roll cake!

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:24.500
It's super delicious!

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:30.010
Oh? It does sound appetizing.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.720
I wanna eat it! Right now!

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.600
Ooshima, go make an Oojima Roll!

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:40.280
Why are you still calling me Ooshima even though you can say "Oojima Roll"?

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:41.120
Yuuki!

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:44.060
How much do you think you could earn with the Oojima Roll?

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:48.300
Let's see. Ingredients would cost about 400 yen per roll.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:51.660
Say we get ten slices from each roll, so that'd be 40 yen each.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:55.040
If we sold it at 100 yen per slice, the profit would be 60 yen each.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:59.440
To raise at least 30,000 yen, I'd need to make 50 rolls.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.040
I can't make that many!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.140
What? You can't?

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:04.280
It's impossible!

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:09.180
Even if I skip classes to bake the whole day, I won't be able to make more than about 20!

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:13.090
With 20 rolls, we'd only get 12,000 yen in profit.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:16.470
How about we increase the profit per slice?

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:19.240
To raise 30,000 yen...

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:21.430
We'd need to sell each slice at 190 yen!

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:26.020
190 yen would feel pretty expensive for sure.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.880
How about freebies to go with them?

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:31.860
If those freebies cost us money,
that would defeat the point.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.680
So it has to be freebies that don't cost us money?

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:39.160
Shaking hands and taking pictures wouldn't cost us money!

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.560
Who'd pay to shake hands with you, Ooshima?

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:44.710
<i>You'd</i> have to pay <i>me</i>
for a handshake.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:46.310
You people...

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.380
Oh, I've got something.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.500
Whether you could sell is an entirely different issue,

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.880
but I see the general direction of where this could go.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.480
Direction?

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:59.360
A way to sell Oojima Rolls at a high price without adding to our cost.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:03.140
I'll handle the rest, so you just make 20 Oojima Rolls.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.520
So you're telling me to skip class?

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:10.000
Since that's all taken care of, you should think about what to hand out.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:14.200
Huh? It's okay to skip classes for an election campaign?

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.420
I didn't hear anything here.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:17.520
That's dirty.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.330
Bring <i>them</i> here.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.680
Wow!

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.540
These are things we handed out last year.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:30.250
Wouldn't it be considered bribery to hand things out for free?

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:34.300
It's perfectly fine if they're recognized
as the candidate's campaign goods.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.740
Campaign goods?

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:39.420
Notice how all these goods have my name and picture on them?

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.640
I see.

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:45.270
Goods that leave an impression will help people remember your name.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.720
But goods with Ooshima on them...

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.440
Who would want something like that?

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.340
I would!

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.580
Like a shower curtain with Yuuki-senpai on it!

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.320
Shower curtain?

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:55.950
Yes!

00:09:57.170 --> 00:10:00.020
You can put it up and get it wet.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.240
Wet with what?!

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:06.500
But we have neither the money nor the time to make campaign goods.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.500
If they aren't worth anything, people won't accept them, even if they're free.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.880
But it'd cost money and time to make something appealing.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:18.560
Why don't we hand out the snacks we've stocked up in here?

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.430
Using snacks obtained with club funds falls under misappropriation.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:24.100
This is tough.

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:28.280
Yaoi Sticks.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:32.230
All-you-can-eat Yaoi Sticks.

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:37.380
Right, the Yaoi Sticks weren't bought with club funds!

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:40.440
We get them from Yume for free!

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:41.260
Yume!

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:43.440
Yeah, that'd be great, Dad.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:45.540
How many do you need?

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.710
At least 2,000. If possible, 3,000!

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:48.980
You heard that?

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.180
Thanks, Dad!

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:54.560
So we got a hold of 3,000.
They should be here soon.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.710
All right!

00:10:56.190 --> 00:11:00.760
Now the question is how to turn Yaoi Sticks into campaign goods.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.520
Okay, done!

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.640
It doesn't look much like a pamphlet.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:12.120
It has the candidate's name and key issues. A very good pamphlet.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:12.860
Seriously?

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:16.940
Just to be safe, take it to the Election Administration Committee for approval.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:19.360
Ai, Kii, go ask the Election Committee!

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.280
Roger!

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:30.320
What a pair of monkeys.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:33.380
We're not monkeys!

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:38.620
But there isn't enough time to make all 3,000 of them by hand.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:41.040
It'd be quick with sticker labels.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:43.080
How much do they cost?

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:45.890
About 1,000 yen for a 20-sheet
pack with 10 labels per page.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:50.380
We'd need 15 sets of that, so that'd cost us 15,000 yen.

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:53.710
That's expensive! We can't afford that!

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:58.820
They're a little small, but you'd only need seven sets if you got the 24-per-page ones.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:00.410
Hello?

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:03.440
Yeah. Okay. Got it.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.860
The Election Committee gave their answer.

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:10.450
People might take it the wrong way if they fall off, so we have to stick them on firmly.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:12.160
So we're in the clear?

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.480
It's all settled.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:17.570
So, Hazuki, mind lending us campaign funds?

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:23.090
Teachers are forbidden from giving
financial assistance to candidates.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.180
<i>Lending</i> money isn't forbidden.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:26.940
All we're doing is borrowing.

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:29.200
We'll give it back once the primaries are over!

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:31.680
Oh? Then for the time being...

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:33.520
Is 30,000 yen good enough?

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:34.820
Why do you keep it there?!

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:38.900
Thank you! No less from the Food Club advisor, Shinonome Hazuki!

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:41.150
Looks like everything is working out fine.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:44.150
Let's go raise those campaign funds!

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.920
Yeah!

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.140
Yeah.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.220
W-We have to put labels on all of these?

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:02.900
This is too much.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:04.430
Never fear!

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.800
This is where Non-chan's invention comes into play!

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:14.940
She thought this might happen and developed this helper machine, Harihari-kun!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.600
That machine is going to put on the labels for us?

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:21.660
No, Harihari-kun is a massage machine

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:24.490
that'll gently massage your shoulders
when they're sore from working!

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.240
Why is it called Harihari-kun?

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:27.740
"Harihari-kun" is short for

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:31.240
hydraulic suspension-linked, posture control and alignment system-equipped,

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:34.250
multi-hand massage manipulator!

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:39.250
It's a brilliant name that also expresses
how it eases hard, stiff shoulders!

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:44.880
So basically, we <i>do</i> have to put the labels on them ourselves.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:47.240
If it takes ten seconds to affix one label,

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:49.320
all of this will take ten hours for one person.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:52.010
However, it'll take only one hour with 10 people.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.300
And the number of people we have is...

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:57.310
I'm a teacher, so I can't help.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:14:02.190
Sumiyoshi-san and Yumeshima-kun will come with me to help set up the booth.

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.120
Then just five people?

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:05.940
Is Ooshima still not back?

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:11.220
He went out to buy ingredients for 20 Oojima Rolls, so he'll take a while.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.040
Yuu-chan is doing his share of the work!

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.200
It's time for everyone else to work hard!

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:19.100
Let's do this!

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:22.500
So heavy.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:25.510
I should've brought Yume with me or something.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:30.220
These guys are running just so they can sell stuff, huh?

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.460
Isn't this a violation of the Washington Convention?

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:48.610
Hey, hey! What's the meaning of this?!

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:51.570
Yeah, yeah! What's the meaning of this, you twat?

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.700
Is that... Shinonome-san?

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:58.180
Hey, hey, hey! What do you mean by "cutting our club funds"?

00:14:58.180 --> 00:15:00.330
Yeah, yeah! What do you mean?!

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:05.090
We're a club with a long history of fine achievements! You hear me?!

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.860
Whoa, I should stop them.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:10.440
You've got some nerve, picking a fight with the Air Sumo Club!

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:11.720
"Air Sumo Club"?

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:20.270
Hey! I'm the very first champion
of air sumo, Sorasou Ryuuzeki!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:25.140
We have a champion! Isn't that enough of an achievement?

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.030
Sorasou Ryuuzeki-san!

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:32.530
We've found some suspicious entries in your club expenditures.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.030
Wh-What?

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:38.000
The majority of the club funds are going towards sumo stew,

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:41.710
but is that much stew a necessity for air sumo?

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.960
If you intend to practice air sumo, why not eat air sumo stew as well?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.760
Wh-What?

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.220
Are you telling us to eat mist or something?

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:53.720
Yes, you should perfect the art of the air.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:55.970
C-Cu-Cu-Cu-Cu...

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:58.320
Playing air chicken this time?

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:00.230
Curse you!

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:02.180
Hey, bring salt!

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:03.190
Aye, sir!

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:07.570
Get out! Go! Go!

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:11.070
Never come back again! Go! Go!

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.490
A-Air salt?

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:15.360
If you'll excuse me...

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:23.500
She was too much for me to handle!

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:25.620
Oh.

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:28.300
Hello.

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:30.800
How many more?

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.930
<b>Stop
the club
reforms</b>
<b>Oojima
Yuuki
There's still a whole bunch left.</b>

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:35.550
This is daunting.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:00.080
Are you okay?

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:03.210
Normal.

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:08.460
I keep finding budgets wasted on trivial things with each investigation.

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:11.500
In order to reduce these wasted resources,

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.970
I need to continue conducting investigations.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:16.280
Even while you're running an election campaign?

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:18.540
I'm still the Finance Commissioner, after all.

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.470
The presidential election and my work are unrelated.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.340
You're pretty strict.

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:26.460
But it's undeniable that there are many clubs with questionable activities.

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:28.480
No, that's not what I meant.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:30.360
You're too strict on yourself.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.500
It's not as bad as you think.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:35.450
But...

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:38.450
I'm just being stubborn.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:39.740
Huh?

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:45.720
As you're aware, Takafuji Academy respects the independence of its students,

00:17:45.720 --> 00:17:48.750
so most of the administrative authorities rest upon the student body.

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:54.820
The student council is practically in charge of governing a small nation called Takafuji Academy.

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:59.640
If we govern it too leniently, the academy will quickly collapse.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.780
Like I said, you're strict.

00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:04.740
I don't think the financial situation of the academy

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:07.140
is severe enough to require so many budget cuts.

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:10.270
Have you thoroughly gone through my manifesto?

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:15.180
You might have focused too much on the club disbanding and overlooked the rest,

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:18.780
but I would appreciate it if you could peruse the entire platform when you have time.

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:22.240
The club reform isn't solely for budget reduction.

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:23.200
Huh?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:37.260
There are still so many left.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:39.300
Will I be able to get it all done today?

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:43.540
The Student Council President, huh?

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:45.700
Oojima-senpai is amazing.

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:47.220
Oh?

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:51.060
You know someone that amazing?

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:53.840
Come with us for a sec.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:55.190
Um...

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:56.980
We want to hear more.

00:18:56.980 --> 00:18:59.280
I still have work to do.

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:00.490
You were slacking off just now.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.960
You don't want to hang out with us?

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:06.200
I...

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:16.630
Mii-chan, let me see that.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:19.300
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:20.630
What's going on, Yuu-kun?

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:23.890
Shinonome Satsuki's manifesto...

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:25.510
<u><b>Harassment Issue</b>
Reform of Financial Aid System</u>

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:26.640
Here it is!
<u><b>Harassment Issue</b>
Reform of Financial Aid System</u>

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:31.540
Reform of the financial aid system?

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:44.950
<b>Discontinuation of the financial aid system</b>

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.260
All that work tired me out.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:05.600
Yeah, I don't want to see another Yaoi Stick for a while.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:09.720
But we got all those done on time, and we're almost done setting up the booth.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:12.760
Now we just need you to do a good job writing the speech!

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:14.800
That'll be tough.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:17.880
Hm? What's wrong, Yuuki?

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:20.560
He's been like that ever since he came back from shopping.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.680
Aomi-san!

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:31.000
Huh? That's the girl who ran into you the other day.

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:33.100
Aomi-san,

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:36.100
are you looking for something?

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:37.880
No, I'm fine.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.680
Is it something important? Would you like some help?

00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:43.680
No. Really, I'm fine.

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:46.510
It's getting dark, so we should look for it togeth—

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:47.640
I'm fine!

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:52.060
Sorry.

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.640
I'm... fine.

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:57.230
Really.

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:12.810
Okay, you go ahead and eat.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:15.860
Sorry. I'll be back as soon as I can.

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:16.660
See you.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:32.680
<i>You piss me off so much.</i>

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:37.660
Were you trying to show off that you know an upperclassman? Huh?

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:39.360
No, I wasn't...

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.900
<i>I bet you gave him the eye.</i>

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:44.570
It would work even better without this!

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:47.080
P-Please stop!

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:49.080
<i>Ew, look at this!</i>

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:50.380
<i>What should we do with this?</i>

00:21:50.380 --> 00:21:52.200
<i>Let's throw it away. It's just trash.</i>

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.660
<i>Good idea.</i>

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:24.620
In the classroom, looking out the window,
kyoushitsu no madobe de nagameru

00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:28.570
Watching the sky fade softly into twilight,
yasashii yuugure no sora

00:22:28.570 --> 00:22:32.670
I turn around, and there you are again
furimukeba kimi ga egao de

00:22:32.670 --> 00:22:36.750
Looking at me, you smile
kocchi wo miteta

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:41.090
"Let's go home," you always say,
issho ni kaerou itsumo no

00:22:41.090 --> 00:22:45.260
Going all the places we go every day
toomawari wo shinagara

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:49.180
Your fingers are just a step away
mada sukoshi todokanai

00:22:49.180 --> 00:22:55.770
But deep inside me, it hurts not holding your hand
yubisaki ga tada setsunakute

00:22:57.430 --> 00:23:02.410
In my heart, I found all these hopes and dreams
ano hi kimi to meguriaeta kara

00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:06.580
Because on that day we happened to meet
takusan no yume wo mitsuketan da

00:23:06.580 --> 00:23:08.810
Even when I wanted to cry,
nakitai toki demo

00:23:08.810 --> 00:23:12.460
You always stayed right there by my side
itsumo soba ni ite kurete

00:23:12.460 --> 00:23:14.990
I want to thank you so much
doumo arigatou

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:19.260
What I wrote on that page I hid from you
no-to ni kaita himitsu no pe-ji wa

00:23:19.260 --> 00:23:23.130
Were the words that I just couldn't say
zutto iezu ni ita kotoba

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:28.890
Now they float forever as whispers on the wind
ima kaze no naka zutto sasayaku yo nee

00:23:28.890 --> 00:23:36.770
Listen close, it says, "I love you so much"
kiite kimi ga daisuki da yo

00:23:42.890 --> 00:23:44.900
Have any recommendations for a homemade snack recipe?

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:48.840
Take some bread crust, deep fry it, and sprinkle on some sugar. It's delicious and cheap!

00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:50.580
How about something that looks better?

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:54.740
Take some bread crust and fry it with margarine and sugar. It's delicious and cheap!

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:56.660
No, something that looks more intricate.

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:58.920
Take some bread crust, put it on the stove until it's crisp,

00:23:58.920 --> 00:24:02.360
then mix it with sugar, and you get <i>karintou</i>! It's cheap, too!

00:24:02.360 --> 00:24:04.170
Something other than bread crust!

00:24:04.170 --> 00:24:06.880
Next time, Episode 5: Festival.

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:11.260
You can even make gratin or pudding with it. It's a magical ingredient, and cheap!
